[about]
Title=09 - Glossary
Intro=The words the kit uses, in alphabetical order. I say the term; the reader says what it means. Each is one line, for looking up or for listening straight through.
Setup=Nothing is needed.
Homework=Pick five terms you did not know and find each one in the kit or an app.

[step]

Say=accept dot inix.
Key=
Hear=An app's acceptance checks: a name and a command each, run by check and reported in the evidence.

[step]

Say=access letter.
Key=
Hear=The underlined letter in a caption, from the first letter of a word, one per dialog or menu; the check counts them.

[step]

Say=app.
Key=
Hear=A program built on the kit: DbDo, EdSharp, FileDir, HomerScribe, and any made with newHomerApp.

[step]

Say=build.
Key=
Hear=The command that puts an app's files in order, speaks its tutorials, compiles it and makes its installer, logging every stage.

[step]

Say=Camel Type.
Key=
Hear=The coding style the kit's skill teaches: a prefix on every name saying its type, lower camel case, constants with c underscore.

[step]

Say=check.
Key=
Hear=The command that refuses what release would refuse: encoding, access letters, keys, the Local tree, hotkeys, tutorials, acceptance.

[step]

Say=evidence.
Key=
Hear=The Markdown report check writes, saying what was checked and what it found.

[step]

Say=finish page.
Key=
Hear=The installer's last page: optional pieces as boxes, each saying Install, Update or Reinstall, with a results box after.

[step]

Say=fixEncoding.
Key=
Hear=The script that puts every file in the Homer encoding: UTF-8 with a byte order mark, CRLF line endings.

[step]

Say=Homer encoding.
Key=
Hear=UTF-8 with a byte order mark and CRLF line endings, for every text file the kit or an app ships.

[step]

Say=Homer Player.
Key=
Hear=The player shared by every Homer program: a track list, Scroll Lock to pause, sliders, Alt plus Shift plus R to record.

[step]

Say=HomerComponents dot iss.
Key=
Hear=The shared installer script: the finish page, the three states, the results box, from a ten-line table in the app.

[step]

Say=hotkeys.
Key=
Hear=Every command with its key, listed three ways -- by menu, by key, by command -- generated from the program itself.

[step]

Say=inix.
Key=
Hear=The settings file format: sections and lines, read by the Inix class, with comments that make the file its own documentation.

[step]

Say=Lbc.
Key=
Hear=Label before control: the class that builds every Homer dialog, with Tab, Alt letters, Control plus Enter and Escape.

[step]

Say=Local tree.
Key=
Hear=Where an app keeps its data, settings and logs: under local application data, never Roaming.

[step]

Say=LocalFiles.
Key=
Hear=The policy file naming the files that stay on the author's machine and never travel to the repository.

[step]

Say=newHomerApp.
Key=
Hear=The command that makes a new app from the template: its folder, its files, its twelve tutorial skeletons.

[step]

Say=pattern of twelve.
Key=
Hear=The walks every app has: overview, install, interface, keys, up to five tasks, glossary, conclusion, more information.

[step]

Say=release.
Key=
Hear=The command that checks, commits, pushes, tags and publishes the installer on GitHub, refusing when it should.

[step]

Say=RepoFiles.
Key=
Hear=The policy file naming the files that travel to the repository, so a stray one is noticed.

[step]

Say=Say layer.
Key=
Hear=The question keys: Shift or Alt with a letter, speaking a fact and changing nothing; twice, the words in a window.

[step]

Say=session log.
Key=
Hear=What a program did this session, one file per run, under its logs folder in the Local tree.

[step]

Say=skill.
Key=
Hear=A folder of instructions an AI assistant reads to learn the kit's rules: coding, tutorials, installers, documents.

[step]

Say=template.
Key=
Hear=A database or document an app ships and copies to the data folder the first time it is opened; the copy is the person's.

[step]

Say=walk.
Key=
Hear=One spoken tutorial: a text file of steps in four beats, spoken by the build in two voices.

[step]

Say=Twenty-six terms. The guide, HomerDev dot md, has each of them in context.
Key=
Hear=
